{"name":"Corn Poppy Cherry","hex":"#ee4411","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"corn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any cereal plant (or its grain) that is the main crop or staple of a country or region.","Maize, a grain crop of the species Zea mays."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To granulate; to form (a substance) into grains.","To preserve using coarse salt, e.g. corned beef."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corn"},{"term":"poppy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the genus Papaver or the family Papaveraceae, with crumpled, often red, petals and a milky juice having narcotic properties; especially a common poppy or corn poppy (Papaver rhoeas) which has orange-red flowers; the flower of such a plant.","A bright red colour tinted with orange, like that of the common poppy flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright red colour tinted with orange, like that of the common poppy flower (Papaver rhoeas)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poppy"},{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Papaver rhoeas","blocks":[{"text":"Papaver rhoeas, with common names including common poppy, corn poppy, corn rose, field poppy, Flanders poppy, red poppy, and Odai, is an annual herbaceous species of flowering plant in the poppy family Papaveraceae. It is native to north Africa and temperate Eurasia and is introduced into temperate areas on all other continents except Antarctica."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Papaver_rhoeas_Lincolnshire_2026.jpg/330px-Papaver_rhoeas_Lincolnshire_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papaver_rhoeas"},{"title":"Maize","blocks":[{"text":"Maize, also known as corn, is a tall stout grass that produces cereal grain. The leafy stalk of the plant gives rise to male inflorescences or tassels which produce pollen, and female inflorescences called ears. The ears yield grain, known as kernels or seeds. In modern commercial varieties, these are usually yellow or white; other varieties can be of many colors. Maize was domesticated by indigenous peoples in southern Mexico about 9,000 years ago from wild teosinte. Native Americans planted it alongside beans and squashes in the Three Sisters polyculture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Zea_mays_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-283.jpg/330px-Zea_mays_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-283.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maize"},{"title":"Poppy","blocks":[{"text":"A poppy is a flowering plant in the subfamily Papaveroideae of the family Papaveraceae. Poppies are herbaceous plants, often grown for their colourful flowers. One species of poppy, Papaver somniferum, is the source of the narcotic drug mixture opium, which contains powerful medicinal alkaloids such as morphine and has been used since ancient times as an analgesic and narcotic medicinal and recreational drug. It also produces edible seeds. Following the trench warfare in the poppy fields of Flanders, Belgium, during World War I, poppies, specifically the red poppy, have become a symbol of remembrance of soldiers who have died during wartime, especially in the UK, Canada, Australia, Africa and other Commonwealth realms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Poppies_in_the_Sunset_on_Lake_Geneva.jpg/330px-Poppies_in_the_Sunset_on_Lake_Geneva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poppy"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Papaver_rhoeas_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-101.jpg/330px-Papaver_rhoeas_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Papaver_rhoeas_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-101.jpg/330px-Papaver_rhoeas_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoeh-101.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Poster_papaver_3a.jpg/500px-Poster_papaver_3a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Poster_papaver_3a.jpg/1280px-Poster_papaver_3a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Poster_papaver_3a.jpg/500px-Poster_papaver_3a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The three stages in a common poppy flower: bud, flower, and capsule","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APoster_papaver_3a.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Papaver_rhoeas_capsules.jpg/500px-Papaver_rhoeas_capsules.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_